 <section id="accounts" tabindex="-1"><h2>Accounts</h2>
 <p>Creating an account requires your name, email address and password. Supabase Auth manages authentication and password security. We store your business name, type, country, time zone and ownership link when you set up a business. Without the required details, we cannot create or operate your account.</p>
 <p>We use this information to verify your email, sign you in, save your settings and help recover access. Verification and password-reset emails are account security messages sent through Resend. Creating an account does not join the waitlist or subscribe you to marketing.</p>
-<p>Only business details you explicitly publish are intended to appear on the public business website. Saving a draft does not publish it. Review public contact details and images before publishing.</p></section>
+<p>Only business details you explicitly publish are intended to appear on the public business website. Saving a draft does not publish it. A deliberately published preview website is also public; a preview label is not an access restriction. Review public contact details and images before publishing.</p></section>
 <section id="enquiries" tabindex="-1"><h2>Enquiries and quote requests</h2>
 <p>The enquiry form collects your name, email address and/or phone number, your selected service if supplied, and what you need. Your name, at least one contact method and the requested description are required so the selected business can respond.</p>
 <p>FaraiOS stores the submitted enquiry privately for that business owner. The business uses it to answer questions, discuss requirements and prepare a quote. It is not posted publicly or shared with other businesses through the public page. An enquiry does not create a confirmed booking, a FaraiOS account or marketing consent.</p>
