 <section id="storage" tabindex="-1"><h2>Providers and retention</h2>
 <p>FaraiOS uses Supabase for authentication and stored records, Plesk-managed website hosting, and Resend for relevant emails. The current Supabase project is hosted in Ireland. Hosting, email, security logs and backups may involve processing in other countries.</p>
-<p>Account information is kept while your account is active. Enquiries and service records remain available for the business’s follow-up and administration; they do not currently have an automatic deletion period matching the waitlist. Ask the business or FaraiOS about access, correction or deletion. We will explain where records need to be retained for service administration, legal obligations or dispute handling. Logs, backups and copies outside the platform can have different retention periods.</p></section>
+<p>Account information is kept while your account is active. Enquiries and service records remain available for the business’s follow-up and administration; they do not currently have an automatic deletion period matching the waitlist. Ask the business or FaraiOS about access, correction or deletion. We will explain where records need to be retained for service administration, legal obligations or dispute handling. Logs, backups and copies outside the platform can have different retention periods.</p>
+<p>Unpublishing a website removes its current public page but retains the private draft and business records. Deactivating staff access, cancelling a booking or voiding an invoice preserves the related history; it is not account deletion. Financial corrections and audit records are retained so that previous actions remain explainable. There is currently no automatic account or business-record purge.</p>
+<p>For a closure or deletion request, we record the information requested, the action agreed, any information that must remain, the reason and a review date. We explain the outcome rather than promise immediate deletion of every copy. Backup recovery and retention coverage are being reviewed separately; this notice does not promise that a deletion instantly removes historical backups. Copies held by a service business or email recipient need separate handling.</p></section>
 <section id="rights" tabindex="-1"><h2>Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
 <p>Contact the business about its customer or service records, or <a href="mailto:hello@faraios.com">hello@faraios.com</a> about your FaraiOS account, waitlist or platform privacy concern. You can ask what information is held, request access or correction, request deletion, or object to processing where applicable. We may need to verify your identity before disclosing or changing private information.</p>
 <p>Waitlist withdrawal stops those marketing updates; it does not delete a product account or cancel a service booking. To change a booking or enquiry, contact the business. Removing a browser draft does not remove a request already submitted.</p>
 <p>If a privacy concern remains unresolved, you can contact South Africa’s <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za/popia/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Regulator</a> for information about complaints. Other rights may apply depending on your location and circumstances.</p></section>
 
+<section id="export" tabindex="-1"><h2>Request a data export</h2>
+<p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@faraios.com">hello@faraios.com</a> with the subject “Data export”, the account email, business name and the information you need. Do not send passwords, sign-in codes or identity documents with your first message. A business name, booking reference or confidential document link alone is not proof of identity.</p>
+<p>Farai Chitekedza is responsible for coordinating these requests. Support is covered Monday–Friday, 08:00–17:00, Africa/Johannesburg. Normal acknowledgement is within one business day; critical incidents are acknowledged within one covered hour. Outside these hours, help is best effort. Acknowledgement is not a promise that an export or closure is already complete.</p>
+<p>We verify your identity and authority, agree the records and period, and give you a request reference and expected next update. A business owner may request its business records; a customer or staff member receives only information they are entitled to receive, after review of other people’s information. Contact the service business first about records it controls; FaraiOS can help direct the request.</p>
+<p>Exports are prepared manually. The standard business export is structured JSON covering agreed business settings, website drafts and published snapshots, services and images, customers, enquiries and activity, requests, quotes, bookings, staff and assignments, invoices, manual payments, invoice history and memberships. Account details and any additional relevant records are handled separately within the agreed scope. Passwords, authentication credentials, confidential-link tokens and other businesses’ private records are excluded.</p>
+<p>We check the scope and completeness before arranging private delivery to the verified recipient. We do not place exports on a public website or send private records merely because someone knows an email address. We explain omissions, available formats, any additional work and the next update before closing the request.</p></section>
+<section id="closure" tabindex="-1"><h2>Request account closure</h2>
+<p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@faraios.com">hello@faraios.com</a> with the subject “Account closure” and your account email and business name. Closure is a manual, verified process. Sending the request does not immediately disable access, unpublish a website, cancel work, stop all messages or erase records.</p>
+<p>We confirm whether you want to stop website publication, restrict access, close the account or request deletion, and offer an export before changes. We review open bookings, quotes, unpaid invoices, staff access and scheduled communications with the authorised business owner. We agree the affected accounts, timing and records to retain before acting. Closing a business must not change another business’s access or records.</p>
+<p>Website withdrawal, staff-access revocation, account restriction, confidential document links and pending communications require separate checks. Previously supplied quote or invoice links may remain usable until specifically addressed; signing out or unpublishing a website does not by itself revoke them. We report completed actions, remaining restrictions or retained records, reasons and review dates in the closure confirmation. We do not describe a request as fully closed while an agreed access or communication check remains unresolved.</p>
+<p>Deletion is separate from closure and is reviewed for the information concerned, the business’s instructions and any applicable retention obligations. We do not automatically erase financial or audit history or another person’s records. Waitlist withdrawal remains separate from account closure and service cancellation.</p></section>
